      "writtenOn": "2023-01-14T10:55:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Caller does not need to know the VPN network. NATTSocketKeepalive is not in the API surface. I think this doc explain what this will going to do if automatic keepalive is enabled. or this should not be documented here?\n\nThis is related to a follow up patch(aosp/2379728). When the design is ready in connectivity side, I think the next would switch to new API with automatic on/off enabled. It\u0027s called from IPSec module which is not decided by the process using IPSec. It means that it may be probably default enabled. However, iWLan may not want this to be enabled since they may care the UDP connections. This may probably enable for VPN only, but it could not be controlled by the user of IPSec. So I think it need to be control here. Otherwise, we may need other mechanism to let the user of IPSec to control wether they need to enable automatic keepalive. \n\nDo you have any sugguestion on this?",
      "parentUuid": "4a19a96b_2d2cf2c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 57,
