      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is lacking a large amount of context here. `mPfd` is a protected member of the superclass and I don\u0027t think someone reading this comment is supposed to understand the entire dynamic around that fd (and it\u0027s very far from trivial, since it\u0027s duplicated and managed by this object).\n\nI think the comment should not rely on technical details that it doesn\u0027t explain. That means you can reword this in one of two ways :\n• Either you can explain everything about the lifecycle of `mPfd`\n• Or you can have a general explanation of what this *does* without mentioning `mPfd` at all\nI think the latter is likely preferable because it will be both easier to understand and much shorter.",
