      "writtenOn": "2023-01-13T04:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is exactly what I meant in my comment :\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2334604/11..12/service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/KeepaliveTracker.java#b457\n\nThis is fundamentally changing the semantics of mStopReason, which is now no longer latched, and becomes part of the state of the finite state automaton represented by this class. That means you are multiplying the complexity of this state machine by a large factor.\n\nSo, your new patchset does not address the comment ; I continue to think you have two options\n• Change the state machine in this file, and to comment very carefully what the new state machine looks like. Typically you will need to have handling of the entire state in all places that manage a state transition, and if some place doesn\u0027t need to look at part of the state, you\u0027ll need comments.\n• Do not change the state machine in this file, and handle the additional state elsewhere (e.g. in ConnectivityService).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 453,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 459,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "519ebf3d6862f98e588b61057ab13442724c4c09",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
